# cpmtools disk definition for the Digital Research C (CP/M-86, RC759) floppy
# images published by Datamuseum.dk (DDHF):
#   Bits:30002664  Digital-Research-C-May84.bin   (raw, 1261568 bytes)
#   Bits:30005869  DR_C_v1.11.imd                 (ImageDisk)
#
# Geometry from the DDHF metadata: 77c 2h 8s 1024b.  The first 4 tracks hold
# the CP/M-86 system; the directory is 512 entries; block size 2048.
#
# NOTE (2026-08-17): maxdir MUST be 512, not 256.  The RC759 CCP/M-86 / DR C
# floppy directory holds 512 entries (16 KB = 8 blocks of 2048), including the
# CP/M-3 datestamp SFCB records (status 0x21 in every 4th slot) — verified on the
# raw DDHF disks 30002664 (Digital-Research-C-May84) and 30002725, which both
# carry SFCBs in the second directory block.  With maxdir 256 cpmtools was blind
# to entries 256-511 AND reserved only 4 directory blocks, so cpmcp wrote file
# DATA over the real directory's second half (blocks 4-7), corrupting it.
#
# Usage: run cpmls/cpmcp from a directory containing this file, e.g.
#   cpmls -f drc-rc759 Digital-Research-C-May84.bin

diskdef drc-rc759
  seclen 1024
  tracks 154
  sectrk 8
  blocksize 2048
  maxdir 512
  skew 1
  boottrk 4
  os 3
end
